{"name":"Pretty Please","hex":"#ffccc8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pretty please","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["An emphatic form of please."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretty_please"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pretty Please (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Pretty Please is the first album released by Hector on Stilts in 2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/69/HoS-Pretty_Please_cover_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretty_Please_(album)"},{"title":"Pretty Please (Dua Lipa song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pretty Please\" is a song by English singer Dua Lipa from her second studio album, Future Nostalgia, released on 27 March 2020. The song was written by Lipa alongside Julia Michaels, Caroline Ailin and the sole producer Ian Kirkpatrick. It was created by the writing team during studio sessions, taking shape from the bassline and title. It is a disco-pop, electro-R&B and funk song with a stripped-back production driven by a funky bass. The song has a chill sound, however its meaning is the opposite; in the lyrics, Lipa pleas for stress relief from her lover after promising she will be chill at the beginning of a relationship, before realizing that is unlike her. Several critics commended the production and lyrics."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretty_Please_(Dua_Lipa_song)"},{"title":"Please","blocks":[{"text":"Please is a word used in the English language to indicate politeness and respect while making a request. Derived from shortening the phrase \"if you please\" or \"if it please(s) you\", the term has taken on substantial nuance based on its intonation and the relationship between the persons between whom it is used. In much of the Western world, use of the word is considered proper etiquette, and parents and authority figures often imprint upon children the importance of saying \"please\" when asking for something from an early age, leading to the description of the term as \"the magic word\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Southdown_bus_199_%28KUF_199F%29%2C_2009_Amberley_Bus_Day.jpg/330px-Southdown_bus_199_%28KUF_199F%29%2C_2009_Amberley_Bus_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Please"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Nate_Smith_%28214037%29.jpg/500px-Nate_Smith_%28214037%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Nate_Smith_%28214037%29.jpg/500px-Nate_Smith_%28214037%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Producer Ian Kirkpatrick was inspired by Nate Smith for the percussion of \"Pretty Please\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANate_Smith_(214037).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Julia_Michaels_11_02_2017_-7_%2839242708641%29.jpg/500px-Julia_Michaels_11_02_2017_-7_%2839242708641%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Julia_Michaels_11_02_2017_-7_%2839242708641%29.jpg/1280px-Julia_Michaels_11_02_2017_-7_%2839242708641%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Julia_Michaels_11_02_2017_-7_%2839242708641%29.jpg/500px-Julia_Michaels_11_02_2017_-7_%2839242708641%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Julia Michaels co-wrote \"Pretty Please\" and also sang backing vocal harmonies.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJulia_Michaels_11_02_2017_-7_(39242708641).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7